# Notes — REPLACE:PROGRAM_SLUG

Working notes, deltas, and the retrieval queue for this program.

## Retrieval queue

Concepts due for closed-book recall at the start of a session, per
`standards/mentoring.md` § *Retrieval opening*.

Revisit roughly after 1 session, then 3, then 8. A concept leaves the queue after **two clean
unaided recalls at least a week apart**. A concept the learner cannot retrieve goes back to the
front — that is a re-teach signal, not a failure.

| Concept | Module | Added | Last recalled | Clean recalls | Status |
|---------|--------|-------|---------------|---------------|--------|
| | | | | 0 | queued |

Status: `queued` · `re-teach` · `retired`

